{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-295934-r4515556","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Papri Chaat (Crispy Indian Snack with Potato)","sourcePageId":295934,"sourceRevision":"4515556","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-06-19T03:33:50Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Papri%20Chaat%20(Crispy%20Indian%20Snack%20with%20Potato)&oldid=4515556","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T13:20:09.094Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Medium Difficulty recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes using ajwain","Category:Recipes using all-purpose flour","Category:Recipes using chaat masala","Category:Recipes using chickpea","Category:Recipes using chile flake","Category:Recipes using cumin","Category:Recipes using lemon juice","Category:Recipes using sugar","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Recipes without servings","Category:South Asian recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"19906c11850fb869e1b99d15463e42621a0fa231f79fbe9a99ddac43b9acbfa0","sourceWikitext":"__NOTOC__{{Recipe summary\n| Category = South Asian recipes\n| Difficulty = 3\n}}\n\n{{recipe}}\n\n== Ingredients ==\n\n=== Papri ===\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Cup|cups]] [[Cookbook:All-purpose flour|plain flour]] (maida)\n* 2 level [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] [[Cookbook:Ajwain|carom seeds]] (ajwain)\n* [[Cookbook:Oil and Fat|Oil]]\n\n=== Chaat ===\n* 3 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tablespoons]] tamarind chutney (imli)\n* 25 [[Cookbook:Milliliter|ml]] [[Cookbook:Lemon Juice|lemon juice]]\n* 1 tablespoon [[Cookbook:Sugar|sugar]] (if the tamarind chutney is spicy)\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|teaspoon]] [[Cookbook:Red pepper flakes|red chile flakes]] (or to taste)\n* [[Cookbook:Cumin|Cumin]]\n* [[Cookbook:Chaat Masala|Chaat masala]]\n* 1 medium [[Cookbook:Onion|onion]], finely [[Cookbook:Chopping|chopped]]\n* [[Cookbook:Tomato|Tomato]], chopped\n* Diced [[Cookbook:Potato|potato]], [[Cookbook:Boiling|boiled]] and drained\n* Cooked and drained [[Cookbook:Chickpea|chickpeas]]\n* [[Cookbook:Salt|Salt]]\n* [[Cookbook:Pepper|Pepper]]\n* [[Cookbook:Yogurt|Yoghurt]]\n\n==Procedure==\n\n=== Papri ===\n\n# Combine the flour, ajwain, a dash of oil, salt, and enough water to make a firm [[Cookbook:Dough|dough]].\n# [[Cookbook:Kneading|Knead]] well and [[Cookbook:Dough#Rolling|roll out]] into small thin rounds of about 40mm (1½ inch) diameter, without using flour if possible. Prick with a fork.\n# [[Cookbook:Deep Fat Frying|Deep fry]] in hot oil over medium heat until golden brown and crisp.\n# Cool and store in an air-tight container.\n# Use as required. \n\n=== Chaat ===\n\n# Combine the tamarind chutney and lemon juice in a bowl. Mix well.\n# Mix in the sugar, chili flakes, cumin, and chaat masala.\n# Mix in the onions, tomatoes, potatoes, and chickpeas. Season with salt and pepper to taste.\n# To serve add papri on the top along with yoghurt thinned with a small amount of milk or water.\n# Add some extra tamarind chutney on the top.\n\n== Notes, tips, and variations ==\n\n* Instead of papri, you could use salted crisps or something crispy.\n\n[[Category:South Asian recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using ajwain]]\n[[Category:Recipes using sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chaat masala]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chickpea]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chile flake]]\n[[Category:Recipes using lemon juice]]\n[[Category:Recipes using all-purpose flour]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cumin]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Papri Chaat (Crispy Indian Snack with Potato)","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"2 cups plain flour (maida)","sourceText":"2 cups plain flour (maida)","amountText":"2 cups plain flour (maida)","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"2 level tsp carom seeds (ajwain)","sourceText":"2 level tsp carom seeds (ajwain)","amountText":"2 level tsp carom seeds (ajwain)","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"Oil","sourceText":"Oil","amountText":"Oil","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"3 tablespoons tamarind chutney (imli)","sourceText":"3 tablespoons tamarind chutney (imli)","amountText":"3 tablespoons tamarind chutney (imli)","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"25 ml lemon juice","sourceText":"25 ml lemon juice","amountText":"25 ml lemon juice","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-6","name":"1 tablespoon sugar (if the tamarind chutney is spicy)","sourceText":"1 tablespoon sugar (if the tamarind chutney is spicy)","amountText":"1 tablespoon sugar (if the tamarind chutney is spicy)","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-7","name":"1 teaspoon red chile flakes (or to taste)","sourceText":"1 teaspoon red chile flakes (or to taste)","amountText":"1 teaspoon red chile flakes (or to taste)","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-8","name":"Cumin","sourceText":"Cumin","amountText":"Cumin","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-9","name":"Chaat masala","sourceText":"Chaat masala","amountText":"Chaat masala","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-10","na